    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "So the Beijing Olympic Games do begin this week with the International Olympic Committee continuing really to stay silent on the ongoing genocide in China. Former Greenbury Commander and Republican Congressman Michael Waltz was the first to call for a boycott. One of the United States to stay home, not compete in these Olympics. And he did that in February. So now that the Olympics are almost here, And the concerns have increased, not decreased since that period. He joins me now with this part of the untold story. Congressman, great to have you here. It's always good to talk to you. Thanks for joining me.",
