    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, look, I think this will be the existential question of our time. And certainly in my time in Congress, the Chinese Communist Party just listened to Chairman Xi's speeches, fully plans to replace the United States as a global leader, openly talks about replacing the American dream and everything that comes with that, whether that's freedom of speech or freedom of religion or the ability to chart your own your own path or ability to challenge political leadership with your own individual rights. They want to replace that with a China drink. And he talks about, I mean, they're laying out the path to do that. What you've described is the economic warfare they've engaged in. They deliberately created dependencies and global dependencies. We are dependent on China for 90% of our pharmaceuticals, for 90% of the rare earth minerals that form our modern economy from computer chips to modern coatings and materials to, I mean, even lithium. So the progressive left wants to drive us towards a green economy that makes us dependent on batteries. which makes us",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
